    "cell_layout": "z=0, FULL 8×8 grid. JSON key z{z}_y{cellA}_x{cellB}: cellA = DGROUP 0x4f9e (×8 axis, engine forward for facing 0 = +cellA); cellB = DGROUP 0x4fa0 (×1 axis). Cell index = z*64 + cellA*8 + cellB. N-wall at maze_ptr+0x60, W-wall at maze_ptr+0x120, 2 bits/cell MSB-first. Party is at cellA=5 cellB=7. Forward axis per facing: f0=+cellA, f1=+cellB, f2=-cellA, f3=-cellB. See docs/re/findings/maze-classify-projection.json. CRITICAL (see docs/re/findings/maze-classify-gating.json): this 8×8 grid is REGION 0's wall plane ONLY. The engine resolves cells across MULTIPLE regions (each a separate 64-cell plane) via the fine-coord region tables; emission needs that multi-region data, not just this single grid.",
    "multiRegion_added": "2026-06-04: each frame now carries a multiRegion.depths array (per-depth center/left/right resolved cells across all touched 64-cell planes + perpWall/fwdEdge/special4/orient2/pit). This is the offline input the port needs to DRIVE the depth walk + resolver for all 4 frames. The emit PREDICATE remains OPEN (see maze-classify-gating.json) — the multiRegion data drives the walk, not the emission decision."
